<%# Static help page /workspace/<id>/help: how to use the workspace. -%>
<header class="page-header">
  <div>
    <span class="eyebrow">WORKSPACE GUIDE</span>
    <h1>How can we help?</h1>
    <p>Use the workflow below to keep your business records complete.</p>
  </div>
  <a class="button" href="mailto:<%= helpers.organizationSupportEmail(data.organization) %>">Email support</a>
</header>
<div class="grid-2">
  <section class="card stack">
    <h2>Create your first invoice</h2>
    <ol class="help-list">
      <li>Choose the correct business from the sidebar.</li>
      <li>Review its address, GST registration, bank details and document branding.</li>
      <li>Add a customer, vendor or B2B buyer in Contacts.</li>
      <li>Add catalog products and services, or enter document items directly.</li>
      <li>Create an invoice, choose the issuing GST registration and check its totals.</li>
      <li>Preview the saved document, download its PDF or send it by email.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="<%= helpers.url(data,'invoices','new') %>">Create invoice</a
      ><a class="button" href="<%= helpers.url(data,'customers') %>">Open contacts</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="card stack">
    <h2>Payments &amp; installments</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Open an invoice’s Payments page to record receipts or create an installment schedule. Use an equal EMI,
      down payment, custom amounts or the 70% / 20% / 10% preset.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Configured payment gateways can create and synchronize payment links. If a payment is entered
      incorrectly, void it with a reason; the correction remains in the history.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      A fully paid invoice can be finalized. Issued documents keep their saved customer, issuer and format
      information.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="card stack">
    <h2>Quotations &amp; delivery</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Prepare quotations and proforma invoices before billing. Convert an eligible quotation or proforma into
      an invoice when the customer is ready. Reopening the conversion returns the same linked invoice.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Create a delivery challan from an invoice to carry its items and shipping details. Delivery challans
      show quantities without prices or taxes.
    </p>
    <a class="text-button" href="<%= helpers.url(data,'quotations') %>">Open quotations →</a>
  </section>
  <section class="card stack">
    <h2>Customer statements</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Open Customer ledger to review balances across contacts, then open a statement for its invoices,
      receipts and receipt corrections. Date filters change the statement period; current outstanding
      remains visible separately. Export includes all matching rows, and Print statement opens a complete
      printable copy.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Statements use current invoice status. Older balances without dated receipts are clearly marked;
      opening and running balances are unavailable where the history cannot establish them.
    </p>
    <a class="text-button" href="<%= helpers.url(data,'ledger') %>">Open customer ledger →</a>
  </section>
  <section class="card stack">
    <h2>Follow up on payments</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Payment reminders lists open invoice and installment dates. Preview a reminder to review the saved
      recipient, due date and remaining amount, then choose Queue reminder. Delivery status appears in
      Reminder history. The invoice needs a valid saved email and this business needs an outgoing sender.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Administrators can separately enable automatic reminders and select days before or after each due
      date. The server checks the balance again before first delivery. Missed dates are skipped after
      downtime; an already attempted email may still finish after a payment.
    </p>
    <a class="text-button" href="<%= helpers.url(data,'reminders') %>">Open payment reminders →</a>
  </section>
  <section class="card stack">
    <h2>Recurring invoice drafts</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      An administrator can create a weekly, monthly, quarterly or yearly schedule from a saved invoice.
      The schedule keeps its item and price inputs. Each due occurrence creates a new draft with current
      business and customer details, ready for review before issuing or sending.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      New schedules start paused unless activation is selected. Open a schedule to review its next date,
      generated invoices and activity, or pause and resume it. A failed dependency pauses generation for
      review. Changing the source invoice later does not change the saved schedule template.
    </p>
    <a class="text-button" href="<%= helpers.url(data,'recurring') %>">Open recurring invoices →</a>
  </section>
  <section class="card stack">
    <h2>Access &amp; business identity</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      An administrator approves new team accounts and assigns the businesses each member can access. Use a
      separate login for every team member.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Each business has its own contacts, catalog and document numbering. Independent businesses use their own
      legal identity, payment account and email sender.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Administrators can download verified database snapshots from Database backups. Restored data stays on
      hold until payments, email delivery and accounts have been reviewed. Restored reminder automation is
      disabled and recurring schedules are paused until an administrator reviews and enables them again.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
